Subject: LING: PIE grammar

For those interested in the history of ideas, there is a wonderful reference
dictionary by Carl Darling Buck.  The name of the book escapes me, but
it is organized into semantic categories and gives the attested roots for
words in those categories, in may IE languages.  This book is almost
certainly out of print.  Also, Calvert Watkins' _American Heritage Dictionary
of Indo-European Roots_ is worth checking into, and can probably be obtained
or ordered from your local bookstore.

-- Simon

