From: Elizabeth Schwartz <betsys@ra.cs.umb.edu>
Subject: SELF: Self-transf workshop

My brother went through one of those Forum seminars. He was unbearable
for about a month or two afterwards, as he seemed to be unable to have
a conversation without turning it into pressure to go to a meeting.
  On the other hand, he went back to school, turned pre-med, and has
been on the Dean's list ever since.
  My impression was that the Forum was a great pep talk and that my
brother, who was a talented person unclear of what direction he should
take in his life, got a great deal out of it.
  Personally, at that time I was already working very hard in a
direction I had already chosen (working full-time at my first
professional job, nad finishing my BSCS at night) and I had a strong
sense that I had already learned what the Forum had to teach. I could
use some help with organization (can't we all?) but the Forum would be
overkill for that.
  The Forum might be a useful experience, in this outsider's view, for
